        "heading": "King Salmon",
        "heading_size": "title-md",
        "heading_alignment": "text-center md:items-center",
        "heading_tag": "h2",
        "subheading": "from Ōra King",
        "description": "<p>Ōra King raises <em>Oncorhynchus tshawytscha</em>, also known as Chinook or King salmon—the largest and most prized of the Pacific salmon species. Known for its buttery richness and fine marbling, this species is genetically predisposed to high fat content, resulting in luxurious texture and depth of flavor. In aquaculture, it thrives in cold, oxygenated water, with slower growth cycles that allow time for flavor and structure to develop. For chefs, King salmon offers exceptional versatility—delicate enough for crudo or tartare, but rich enough to hold up on the grill or in a slow roast.</p>",
