    "rich_text_fDqEkm": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "text_e9xqD8": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Ōra King raises its salmon in ocean net pens in the Marlborough Sounds. Every supplier is third-party tested for nutrition, mercury and microplastics, then randomly audited to ensure consistent compliance with the Seatopia Standard.</p><p>Our King Salmon tested at 1,140 mg EPA and 2,290 mg DHA, plus 64 mcg selenium, per 8.5 oz skin-on, sushi-grade portion. Values vary by sample and season.</p><p>When we choose farm partners, we look for farms that manage animal health without antibiotics. Many of our farms have no need for them by design, which is the case with scallops and with many of our land-based recirculating farms. Others have transitioned away entirely: our Atlantic salmon partner, Bakkafrost, has used zero antibiotics since 2004.</p><p>In the rare case of a significant animal health threat, some of our farms reserve the right to use therapeutic antibiotics under veterinary guidance. If that happens, the fish are held for a mandatory withdrawal period so that no trace remains before harvest. Antibiotics on the World Health Organization’s list of drugs critically important to human medicine are not permitted.</p>",
            "text_size": "subtext-md",
            "text_max_size": 32,
            "text_font": "body",
            "secondary_color": false,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "text_e9xqD8"
      ],
      "settings": {
        "custom-class": "",
        "section_id": "",
        "text_alignment": "left",
        "text_alignment_mobile": "center",
        "heading": "",
